.TH "ROARK\-CUSTOMER\-FLOW\-FOLDER\-UPDATE" "1" "" "roark-customer-flow-folder-update" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-customer\-flow\-folder\-update \- Update a customer flow folder
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark customer\-flow folder update
\fIfolder\-id\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Renames, recolors or moves a folder. Send `parentId` to move it, with its flows and subfolders, inside another folder, or null to move it to the top level. Fields you omit are left as they are. Built\-in folders cannot be changed. Customer flows were previously called scenarios.
.SH "API"
PUT /v1/customer\-flow/folder/{folderId}
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIfolder\-id\fR
The folder\-id.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
A new name. Must be unique within the parent folder, ignoring case. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<value>\fR
The color the folder is shown with in the app. Folders share the palette labels use. One of: GREEN, RED, ORANGE, PURPLE, GREY, BLUE, PEACH, TEAL, INDIGO, AMBER, ROSE, CYAN. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
What belongs in this folder. Null clears it. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-parent\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
Moves the folder, with everything in it, inside this folder. Null moves it to the top level; omit it to leave it where it is. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
